// warden_encounter.script — the arena1 warden set-piece: one composite encounter
// that chains all four scripted categories with real content.
//
//   approach  -> the boss waits until a player comes within range (waitplayerradius)
//   cutscene  -> a boss-intro scene plays with the camera tracking THIS boss live
//                (playscene ... self), held for its ~4s duration (waitscene)
//   objective -> the mission objective "Kill the warden" appears (l10n'd)
//   battle    -> the boss stops being scripted-idle and fights autonomously (attack
//                hands it to the Fork-2 BATTLE state; it is a real fightable monster)
//   death     -> killing it completes the objective and opens the exit
//
// The boss is the visor archetype, spawned at runtime (Script_SpawnDriven binds
// the character) — arena1.ent is never touched. Its nav marker and the exit are
// runtime-spawned entities resolved by NAME, so a future authored map entity of
// the same name would satisfy the same lookup.
//
// The boss is made invulnerable (invuln 1) for its intro cutscene and back to
// mortal (invuln 0) only once the objective is armed and it enters battle — so
// the player can never kill it before the objective exists, and the cinematic
// reads correctly (the warden cannot die during its own intro).
spawn {
    print warden-armed
    waitplayerradius 400
    print warden-approached
    invuln 1
    playscene warden_intro self
    waitscene 4000
    print warden-cutscene-done
    objective_add objective/kill_warden
    invuln 0
    attack
    print warden-battle-live
}
death {
    print warden-down
    objective_complete 0
    trigger warden_exit_open
    print warden-exit-opened
}
